WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.420
Frozen 2 has been a hit with both adults and
kids alike, and although the movie has plenty

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:10.150
of slapstick comedy for little ones to enjoy,
it also includes some eyebrow-raising grown-up

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:11.770
jokes and references as well.

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:16.740
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video, I'm revealing the 12 most surprising

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:21.240
and shocking adult gags and details that Disney's
animators snuck into Frozen 2.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.840
"Come on, it'll be fun!"

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:26.369
There will be spoilers, so take care if you
haven't seen the movie yet.

00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:28.500
"It began with two sisters."

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.800
When Kristoff sings about proposing to Anna
during 'Some Things Never Change', he gets

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.980
down on one knee and holds up a ring directly
in front of Sven who nods vigorously in reply.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.170
But it's the reaction of the on-lookers to
this scene that makes this a priceless adult

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:46.190
joke, as they clearly think that Kristoff
has taken his theory that 'Reindeer are better

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:50.870
than people' a step too far and is actually
asking one to marry him!

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:54.970
One horrified woman puts her hand in front
of her young daughter's eyes to stop her seeing

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:56.000
what's happening.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.160
While another woman not only turns her head
away from Kristoff and Sven but, as an extra

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.989
precaution, also blocks her eyes with her
hand.

00:01:02.989 --> 00:01:07.010
This isn't the first time the unusual connection
between Kristoff and Sven has been referred

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:08.720
to in the Frozen franchise.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.530
In the first movie, the Trolls poked fun at
their special relationship when they sang

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:16.250
the 'Fixer-Upper' song which included Kristoff's
various flaws such as

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:17.620
'his thing with the reindeer.

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:19.780
That's a little outside of nature's laws!'

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:20.780
"That's normal."

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:25.990
In Frozen 2, Kristoff is of course devoted
to Anna, but the new film still has some funny

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:29.780
callbacks to the original movie’s romantic
tension between the pair.

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:34.229
For example, Elsa and Olaf fall asleep on
their cart ride to the Enchanted Forest, and

00:01:34.229 --> 00:01:38.340
as soon as Anna notices they're no longer
awake, she asks Kristoff what he'd like to

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:39.340
do!

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:43.330
It's clear from both her tone and body language
when she asks the question, and the fact that

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:45.960
she leans in for a kiss, that she's got loving
on her mind.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:46.960
"Yes!"

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:52.670
And then when Kristoff, Olaf, and Sven get
all dressed up in fancy outfits for a special

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:57.180
occasion at the end of the movie, Kristoff
just isn't comfortable with his new clothes,

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.799
and tells Anna, 'You get this for one hour'.

00:01:59.799 --> 00:02:04.170
That's when Anna whispers her rather racy
reply to him, 'That's ok, I prefer you in

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:05.470
leather anyway!'

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:07.229
"Charmed, I'm sure."

00:02:07.229 --> 00:02:12.169
That's followed by even more double-entendres
as Olaf's innocent comment to Kristoff that

00:02:12.169 --> 00:02:17.069
'I'm shocked you can last an hour' will doubtless
be understood by some adults watching as a

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:21.379
reference to something other than the character's
smart new clothes, especially given Anna's

00:02:21.379 --> 00:02:23.249
previous comment about leather.

00:02:23.249 --> 00:02:24.249
"Don't patronise me."

00:02:24.249 --> 00:02:29.049
After the gang encounter the wind spirit in
the Enchanted Forest, it lifts Olaf up in

00:02:29.049 --> 00:02:31.599
the air, twirling him around playfully.

00:02:31.599 --> 00:02:36.709
And as he whirls around, his bottom half billows
out around him, like a dress caught in the

00:02:36.709 --> 00:02:37.709
breeze.

00:02:37.709 --> 00:02:42.019
This is a tribute to the iconic scene in director
Billy Wilders' film The Seven Year Itch where

00:02:42.019 --> 00:02:47.450
Marilyn Monroe's white dress blows up around
her after a blast of air from a subway grate.

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:52.340
And Olaf even remarks that the breezy experience
is 'delicious', just like Monroe did in the

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:55.379
1955 classic comedy about marital infidelity.

00:02:55.379 --> 00:02:57.220
"Ooh, do you feel the breeze from the subway?

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.220
Isn't it delicious?"

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:01.739
Later, when Olaf first introduces himself
to the people trapped in the Forest, Ryder

00:03:01.739 --> 00:03:04.359
gasps and hides behind his sister Honeymaren.

00:03:04.359 --> 00:03:05.769
"Who are you?"

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:07.189
"Hi, I'm Olaf."

00:03:07.189 --> 00:03:11.659
Although Ryder's clearly shocked to meet a
talking snowman, that never occurs to Olaf

00:03:11.659 --> 00:03:14.489
who thinks the problem is something quite
different.

00:03:14.489 --> 00:03:15.489
"Oh!

00:03:15.489 --> 00:03:17.890
Sorry, yeah I just find clothes restricting."

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:22.079
Yes, Olaf believes that Ryder's so stunned
when they meet because he thinks the little

00:03:22.079 --> 00:03:24.129
snowman isn't wearing any clothes!

00:03:24.129 --> 00:03:28.969
So, now we know for sure that, despite the
three stones resembling buttons on his front,

00:03:28.969 --> 00:03:30.959
Olaf actually prefers to go au naturel!

00:03:30.959 --> 00:03:36.430
And just before we get to Elsa's hilarious
adult moment in Frozen 2, I want to let you

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:41.309
know that thanks to this video's sponsor NordVPN,
all our viewers can get a very special Black

00:03:41.309 --> 00:03:47.689
Friday deal of 84% off, plus 4 bonus months
